    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Continental Glaciers cover expansive land masses such as Antarctica and Greenland, moving outwards in all directions.",
        "Valley or Alpine Glaciers are confined within mountain valleys and flow downslope under the influence of gravity.",
        "Piedmont Glaciers occur when valley glaciers emerge from mountain canyons onto adjacent flat plains.",
        "Cirque Glaciers occupy amphitheater-shaped basins high on mountain slopes and often form tarn lakes upon melting."
      ],
